It is Friday evening and the doorbell rings.
Sabine is standing in the hallway with her small dog Bruno.
She is going away this weekend.
She brings his basket and a large bag with her.
"Here is his dog food, his lead and his favourite toy," Sabine says quickly.
I take the bag and put it on the floor.
Sabine immediately explains the rules for the weekend to me.
"You must feed him twice a day," she emphasizes.
"And he is not allowed to sleep on the bed!"
Bruno wags his tail and sniffs my shoes.
"Do not worry, Sabine," I reassure my friend.
"I will take very good care of him."
"Please do not let him run without a lead!" she says seriously.
I smile and look down at Bruno.
"I will feed him," I say.
Sabine says a warm goodbye to us.
"Bye, you two!" she calls.
Then she walks down the stairs and sets off on her trip.
